## Chunk 6 design

### EffortProfile::tree_learn_seeds_for(effort)
  e0..=9 → 1  (unchanged; libjxl single-seed; e ≤ 9 hash-locks
              byte-identical because every seeded helper holds
              canonical for seed 0)
  e10   → 2  (unchanged from chunks 2-5)
  e11   → 16 (was 8 at chunk 5 — chunk 6 doubling, two new
              variance dimensions get their own 4-seed slots)

### Seed-slot layout (16 seeds at e11)

| seed | sample-fraction       | predictor-order            | max_property_values  | properties truncation |
|------|----------------------|---------------------------|---------------------|----------------------|
| 0    | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 1    | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 2    | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 3    | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 4    | Some(0.40)           | perm[0] (canonical)       | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 5    | Some(0.60)           | perm[1] (strong-first)    | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 6    | Some(0.70)           | perm[2] (directional-first)| canonical (256)    | full (canonical)     |
| 7    | None                 | perm[3] (full-reverse)    | canonical (256)     | full (canonical)     |
| 8    | None                 | canonical                 | **Some(64)**        | full (canonical)     |
| 9    | None                 | canonical                 | **Some(128)**       | full (canonical)     |
| 10   | None                 | canonical                 | **Some(192)**       | full (canonical)     |
| 11   | None                 | canonical                 | None (canonical)    | full (canonical)     |
| 12   | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | **Some(8)**          |
| 13   | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | **Some(10)**         |
| 14   | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | **Some(12)**         |
| 15   | None                 | canonical                 | canonical (256)     | None (canonical)     |

Chunk-3 perturbations (`derive_seeded_params`, `derive_seeded_stride`)
remain active for ALL 16 seeds — they cycle by `seed % 4` so every
chunk-6 seed inherits the chunk-3 perturbation pattern from its mod-4
position.

### Why these two dimensions (and not max_tree_depth / property_gain
### threshold per the original brief)
TreeLearningParams has no `max_tree_depth` knob — the greedy builder
grows until no split clears `split_threshold` or `max_nodes` is hit.
The acceptance-threshold dimension is already exercised by chunk-3's
`split_threshold` jitter. `max_property_values` (split granularity)
and `properties.len()` (set size) are the next two structurally
orthogonal knobs that change which trees the greedy builder can reach
without recombining chunk-3's existing perturbations.

### Strict-slot-range gates
Both new helpers return `None` outside their 4-seed slot ranges:
  - `derive_seeded_max_property_values(seed)`: returns None for
    seed < 8 or seed >= 12.
  - `derive_seeded_properties_truncation(seed)`: returns None for
    seed < 12 or seed >= 16.

This codifies the chunk-3..chunk-6 seed-slot doctrine — each chunk's
dimension owns its own 4-seed block; the two chunk-6 dimensions
never stack on a single seed. A `test_chunk6_dimensions_are_orthogonal`
unit test enforces this invariant.

### Expectation
- e9:  byte-identical to chunks 2-5 / pre-RFC#45-chunk-2.
- e10: byte-identical to chunks 3-5 (still 2 seeds, both reserved
  for chunk-3-only perturbations; chunk-4/5/6 helpers no-op).
- e11: strictly ≥ chunk 5 by construction. Seeds 0..=7 cover the
  same candidate space as chunk-5 (chunk-6 helpers held to canonical
  no-op via the seed < 8 gate). The chunk-2 `estimate_token_cost`
  picker keeps the cheapest of the 16 candidate trees — additional 8
  chunk-6 candidates can only improve.

