## Win analysis
Only 1 of 5 cells improved at e11 (1025469 by -334 bytes); other 4 are
byte-identical to chunk 5. This is the expected pattern given chunk-5's
diminishing-returns regime — when chunks 0..=7 cover the relevant
candidate space well, chunk-6's additional 8 candidates can only beat
the picker on images whose minima lie at coarser-bucket-grid or
truncated-property-set tree shapes. 1025469 picked up such a
candidate (likely a bucket-grid coarser variant in seeds 8..=11, since
the chunk-3 perm-rotation already exercised property reordering in
seeds 0..=3). 4 byte-identical cells means chunk-5's best tree was
already optimal among the 16 chunk-6 candidates for those images.

